# KWin's screen locker in Hearth's KWin session (docs/KWIN-INPUT.md). Mantel decides when to lock (Super+L, the power
# menu, Settings › Sign-in › Lock when waking, idle): Lock.qml asks KWin's locker, so KWin itself never locks on its
# own (that would be a setting changing by itself) and the screen it shows is Hearth's (kwin-lock/, installed as the
# look-and-feel package org.hearth.mantel-lock). Read from XDG_CONFIG_DIRS: nothing here is written to your files.
[Daemon]
Autolock=false
LockOnResume=false
Timeout=0

[Greeter]
Theme=org.hearth.mantel-lock
